{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774143177,"nonce":"ucQAdNNK3IS5gtghiJ4wzevcFeM=","message":"**Workflow variant: analysis-first pipeline**\n\nSlightly different from the base pattern. Used when user provides detailed UX feedback that needs interpretation:\n\n1. Opus + Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview independently **analyze** the feedback + codebase (NOT spec — just direction-setting)\n2. Synthesize their analyses\n3. One Opus agent produces **high-level specs** for each partition\n4. One Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview agent **critiques** the spec\n5. One Opus agent per partition **implements** it\n6. One Gemini agent per partition **critiques** the implementation (serial)\n7. One Opus + one Gemini agent do a **final integration critique** (parallel)\n8. Synthesize → final integration → auth request\n\nKey difference from the base pattern: the first round is analysis/direction-setting, not speccing. This is appropriate when the user's feedback is detailed and conversational (with contradictions/revisions) and needs interpretation before speccing.","files":null}]}